Summary
Chain Rule Concept: Differentiates composite functions by taking the derivative of the outer function and multiplying it by the derivative of the inner function.
Steps: Identify inner/outer functions, differentiate each, and multiply.
Applications: Found in many fields including physics, economics, and biology.
This step-by-step approach ensures that you correctly apply the Chain Rule in any scenario where composite functions arise. Happy differentiating!
